[? if neorevisionism == 1 : {!</tr><td>!} <span style="color: #e42bca;">**Neorevisionist:**</span> {!</td><td>!} [+ neorevisionist_votes +]% {!</td></tr>!} ?]

@coalition_menu

The first matter in the conference is what is to be done regarding the party program. The Center has drafted a new program, a significant shift to the left, though the Left gathered around Levi remains skeptical.

Alternatively, the Görlitz program could be maintained, with revisions to match the changing times. With Heidelberg not even entirely satisfying the party left, this would certainly provoke quite the rebellion.

Max Seydewitz of the left meanwhile has proposed before the conference what would amount to a rejection of coalitions with the bourgeois parties in order to represent the interests of the proletariat in all future struggles without regard to their opinions.

The three programmes are effectively mutually exclusive, and whatever motion triumphs will inevitably be taken as a sign of the direction of our party in the aftermath of Hindenburg’s victory.

How does the Conference vote?

- @heidelberg: Adopt a new party program as written by the Centrists.
- @gorlitz: Retain the Görlitz program, but moderately revised.
- @seydewitz: Seydewitz’s motion is passed by the conference!

@heidelberg
subtitle: The Center ([+ center_votes +]%) [? if center_votes < 50 : - though the Centrists lack a majority, it can still pass as a compromise resolution. ?]
choose-if: reformist_votes < 50
on-arrival: heidelberg_program = 1; center_strength += 5; reformist_strength -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent += 5; dvp_relation -= 5; uspd_relation += 5
go-to: saxon_struggle

The party has adopted the Heidelberg program, written by Karl Kautsky of the party center and representing a return towards the party's Marxist roots. 

@gorlitz
subtitle: The Right ([+ reformist_votes +]%) [? if reformist_votes < 50 : - though the Reformists lack a majority, the trade unions may be convinced. ?]
choose-if: (reformist_votes+labor_votes) >= 50
on-arrival: gorlitz_program = 1; center_strength -= 5; left_strength -= 5; reformist_strength += 10; left_dissent += 20; center_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent -= 5; peoples_party_support += 1; dvp_relation += 5; uspd_relation -= 5; labor_strength += 10 if reformist_votes < 50; center_dissent += 5 if reformist_votes < 50
go-to: saxon_struggle

The party has, surprisingly, chosen to retain the bulk of the Görlitz program. The left and center wings of the party are incensed by this decision. [? if reformist_votes < 50 : The trade unions have been given significant concessions to be convinced of this, further angering the centrists. ?]
@seydewitz
choose-if: left_votes >= 50 or ((left_votes+labor_votes >= 50 and not gorlitz_program) or (reformist_votes < 50 and seydewitz_advisor and not gorlitz_program and left_votes+labor_votes >= center_votes and president != "Marx" and dvp_relation < 40 and z_relation < 50))
subtitle: The Left ([+ left_votes +]%) [? if left_votes < 50 : - though the Leftists lack a majority, the trade unions and dissident centrists may be convinced. ?]
on-arrival: left_strength += 20; reformist_strength -= 10; reformist_dissent += 25; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += ((z_relation+dvp_relation)/10); marx_relation -= 10; z_relation -= 15; dvp_relation -= 15; ddp_relation -= 15; uspd_relation += 10; communist_coalition += 1
go-to: saxon_struggle

Surprisingly, the motion to reject cooperation with the bourgeoisie is passed through the conference. The party's right wing is incensed by this decision, with some even threatening revolt.

@saxon_struggle

The next issue for the conference is what should be done about Saxony, where the SPD has essentially split in half following the decision of Max Heldt to govern with the DVP despite the local party chapter's express refusal.

- @get_him_lads: We must expel Heldt for this!
- @a_strongly_worded_note: We must formally condemn Heldt’s actions, but stop short of formal action.
- @leave_heldt_be: Heldt did what he thought was right, even if we disagree. 
- @who_cares: We cannot afford to indulge in this petty intraparty infighting.

@get_him_lads
view-if: reformist_votes < 50
on-arrival: left_strength += 10; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_strength -= 10; reformist_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; in_saxony_spd = 0

A motion to expel Heldt from the party passes. Unfortunately, expelling Heldt from the party does not expel him from the Saxon government and he, alongside a small group styling themselves as the ‘ASPD’, continue in their coalition with the DVP, while our loyalists return to opposition.

- @the_matter_of_the_leadership: Now for the matter of the leadership.

@a_strongly_worded_note
view-if: reformist_votes < 50 and left_votes < 50
on_arrival: left_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 5

We pass a resolution condemning Heldt, but stopping short of actually expelling him. The resolution does not make matters any worse, but nor does it make things any better.

- @the_matter_of_the_leadership: Now for the matter of the leadership.

@leave_heldt_be
view-if: left_votes < 50
on_arrival: reformist_strength += 10; reformist_dissent -= 5; left_strength -= 10; left_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5

The Conference declines to pass any resolution whatsoever.

- @the_matter_of_the_leadership: Now for the matter of the leadership.

@who_cares
view-if: left_votes < 50 and center_votes < 50 and reformist_votes < 50
on_arrival: labor_strength += 10; labor_dissent -= 5; left_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; center_dissent += 3

The Conference turns its attention to other issues.

- @the_matter_of_the_leadership: Now for the matter of the leadership.

@the_matter_of_the_leadership

How does our leadership fare at the Conference?

- @co_leader_1: How does [+ spd_coleader_1_fullname +], of the [+ spd_coleader_1_faction +] faction, fare?

@co_leader_1

How does [+ spd_coleader_1_fullname +], of the [+ spd_coleader_1_faction +] faction, fare?

